layout "layout.faqir"

block content
  p
    | The
    strong backlog
    | holds the factory's
    strong packages
    | : large pieces of work, each one taken from start to finish by one worker. The
    a(href="/docs/projects") project
    | owns its packages. With
    a(href="/docs/autopilot") autopilot
    | on, the server moves them along the line by itself; with it off, a
    a(href="/docs/coordinator") coordinator
    | or you do it by hand. Either way each package's gates are recorded here, and you are asked when something needs
    | you. You watch, answer and, when needed, stop or revert from your phone.

  h2#board The board
  include "partials/shot.faqir" (assets=site.assets file="backlog-desktop.png" alt="The backlog on a desktop: the governor banner with the 5-hour and 7-day usage bars, then six columns of package cards from Backlog to Blocată." caption="The backlog on a desktop, one column per status.")
  p
    | Open
    strong Backlog
    | in the menu. At the top a
    strong project switcher
    | shows all active projects, or just one. On a desktop each status is a column; on a phone you pick a status at the
    | top and see one list. A card shows the package's id and title, the G1 to G5 gate chips, its cost, and these
    | marks:
  ul
    li
      strong ready
      | : it is Gata and everything it depends on is integrated, so it can start now.
    li
      strong waits on …
      | : the packages it still waits for.
    li
      strong sensitive
      | : authentication, access rules, imports or pseudonymisation; such packages get an extra security review and are
      | marked in the digest.
    li An open stop or revert request.
  include "partials/shot.faqir" (assets=site.assets file="backlog-phone.png" alt="The backlog on a phone: the governor banner, a row of status filters with counts, and a list of package cards." caption="On a phone, filter by status." phone)

  h3#statuses The six statuses
  dl
    dt Backlog
    dd Written down, not ready yet.
    dt Gata
    dd Specified and ready to start once its dependencies are integrated.
    dt În lucru
    dd A worker has it.
    dt La porți
    dd The work is done and the gates are running.
    dt Integrată
    dd It passed the gates and was merged. The board shows only what landed in the last day; older packages are archived.
    dt Blocată
    dd It failed the gates three times, or something outside it stops it.

  h3#governor-banner The banner at the top
  p
    | It shows the
    a(href="/docs/coordinator#governor") governor's
    | answer: whether new workers may start, or until when the factory waits, with the 5-hour and 7-day usage and how
    | old that data is.

  h3#archive-link The archive
  p
    | The board shows only packages that are not archived. A package is archived when you or an
    a(href="/docs/operators") operator
    | archives it, when its project is archived, or by itself once it has been integrated for a day (the delay is in
    a(href="/docs/settings#factory") Settings
    | ). Under the board there is a link to each project's archive, its Done tab. See
    a(href="/docs/projects#archive") The archive
    | .

  h2#new Adding packages
  p
    | Use
    strong New task
    | on the board, also from a phone: a title, an optional id (such as
    code P3
    | ; otherwise one like
    code T12
    | is made), a description, the acceptance criteria one per line, what it depends on, its status and its priority.
    | Higher priority starts first among ready packages. Choose the project it belongs to; if the project has an id
    | prefix, it is added to the id (
    code P3
    | becomes
    code ED-P3
    | ). See
    a(href="/docs/projects#ids") Package ids
    | .
  p
    | You can also let the planner write the packages from a goal: see
    a(href="/docs/planning") Planning
    | .

  h3#markdown Importing from Markdown
  p
    | A package can live as a Markdown file in any repository: frontmatter between two
    code ---
    | lines, then the description. Upload the files on the board, or run
    a(href="/docs/commands#tasks-import") bb tasks import
    | with a file or a folder; add
    code --project <key>
    | to import into a project, so its id prefix applies. Importing the same file again updates the package instead of adding a new one. A
    | status in the file only applies while the package is still Backlog or Gata, and a file without dependencies or
    | criteria leaves the existing ones alone.
  pre
    code
      | ---
      | id: P2
      | title: Inventory
      | status: gata
      | depends_on: [P1]
      | priority: 10
      | sensitive: false
      | ---
      | What the package covers.
      |
      | ## Acceptance criteria
      | - Stock moves post to the ledger
      | - The monthly report matches the old one
  p
    code after
    | works as well as
    code depends_on
    | , and the criteria can also be an
    code acceptance
    | list in the frontmatter.

  h3#github Importing GitHub issues
  p
    | With a GitHub token in
    a(href="/docs/settings") Settings
    | , the board can import a repository's open issues, optionally only those with a given label. Pull requests are
    | skipped, and importing again updates the same packages.

  h2#package A package's page
  include "partials/shot.faqir" (assets=site.assets file="task-desktop.png" alt="A package page on a desktop: header with status, branch and cost, the acceptance criteria, and the gates G1 to G5 with verdicts, summaries and a screenshot thumbnail." caption="A package with its gates and their screenshots.")
  p
    | Tap a card to open its page: status (you can change it), repository, branch, cost, the prompt and its version,
    | the Claude Code session and herdr terminal working on it, the acceptance criteria, its dependencies and its full
    | history. When the package is on the line, the page also shows its stage (prepare, qa, build, G1 to G5, cleanup)
    | and what it waits for, and the history lists every move the conductor made and why, as
    code line
    | events.

  h3#gates The gates
  p Each gate shows its latest verdict, its summary and any screenshots; earlier attempts fold away below it.
  dl
    dt G1
    dd Typecheck, lint, unit and end-to-end tests.
    dt G2
    dd Acceptance tests written before the work by another agent, which the worker cannot change.
    dt G3
    dd An independent review with a structured verdict.
    dt G4
    dd Screenshots at desktop and phone width, judged against the design rules.
    dt G5
    dd Rebase on main, then G1 and G2 again on the result.

  h3#stop Stopping or reverting
  p
    strong Oprește pachetul
    | asks whoever is working on this package to stop.
    strong Cere revenirea integrării
    | asks them to revert the package's merge. Both record your request, with an optional note, and the page shows
    | whether it has been picked up yet. With autopilot on, the conductor carries it out: it tells the worker to commit
    | and stop, or runs the revert step on the project's runner. With autopilot off, the coordinator reads the request
    | and does it. The server itself never runs git on your repositories; the runner on your machine does.
  include "partials/shot.faqir" (assets=site.assets file="task-phone.png" alt="A package page on a phone: the gates as a list, followed by the Oprește pachetul and Cere revenirea integrării buttons." caption="The same package on a phone." phone)

  h3#launch Starting a package
  p
    | A package can also be started from its page on one of your machines: as an interactive agent in a new herdr
    | terminal (the default, so it stays visible and correctable), or as a one-shot
    a(href="/docs/jobs") job
    | . Both need the machine's
    a(href="/docs/runner") runner
    | , and the folder must be inside its allowed roots. Launching claims the package at once (it becomes În lucru),
    | so nothing else can hand it to another worker; if the launch fails, it goes back to the status it had.

  h2#decisions Decisions
  include "partials/shot.faqir" (assets=site.assets file="decisions-desktop.png" alt="The Decisions page: a pending question with its context and one button per option, and answered questions below." caption="A question waiting for you.")
  p
    | When something cannot be settled without you, a question arrives as a notification and waits on the
    strong Decisions
    | page (the Inbox links to it, and the attention bar counts it). Tap one of the offered answers or write your own;
    | whoever asked reads it the next time it checks. Cancel a question that no longer matters.
  p The questions come from:
  ul
    li
      strong The conductor
      | (the question is marked
      code factory:line
      | ): a package that needs attention, or the approval to integrate a package before G5. See
      a(href="/docs/autopilot#decisions") What autopilot asks you
      | .
    li
      strong The planner:
      | the plan you approve before its packages become ready. See
      a(href="/docs/planning#approval") Approving a plan
      | .
    li
      strong The gate rounds:
      | a package that failed its last round asks for another round, or to stop.
    li
      strong A coordinator or the foreman,
      | through
      code decision_ask
      | , and launch approvals when an agent key may start workers.
  p
    | An
    a(href="/docs/operators") operator
    | key may answer decisions for you, except its own and launch approvals, which only you answer.
  include "partials/shot.faqir" (assets=site.assets file="decisions-phone.png" alt="The Decisions page on a phone, with option buttons sized for a thumb." caption="Answering from a phone." phone)

  h2#digest The daily digest
  p
    | Once a day, at the time set in Settings → Factory (08:00 by default, the server's time), a notification sums up
    | the last 24 hours: what was integrated, which gates passed or failed, what is in progress or blocked, usage and
    | the governor, and the decisions and requests still waiting, and what operators answered for you. An agent can send one
    | at any time, and so can you from Settings.
